			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Patch desktop.main.js in addition to web.main.js\n\nExtend the ExposeWorkbenchAccessor ESBuild transform to also patch the Electron/Desktop profile's desktop.main.js entry point, not just the web profile's web.main.js. Both files contain the identical instantiation service startup line, but have different first-import markers - web.main.js uses the 'mark' import from performance.js while desktop.main.js uses localize from nls.js. Extract the shared service decorator imports into SharedImportLines to avoid duplication, and add DesktopMainImportMarker/DesktopMainImportReplacement pairs. The match pattern and transform logic are extended to handle both /vs/workbench/browser/web.main.js and /vs/workbench/electron-browser/desktop.main.js. This ensures __CEL_SERVICES__ is populated correctly for the debug-electron and release-electron profiles used at runtime, not just the web profile.",
			"SHA": "11093ba8d18c074bbc8d08572454d6eb96304797"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T22:31:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				221,
				6
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Use static ES imports instead of runtime require() in ExposeWorkbenchAccessor\n\nRefactor the ExposeWorkbenchAccessor ESBuild transform to inject static ES import statements at the top of web.main.js instead of using runtime require() calls to resolve VS Code service modules. The transform now anchors on the stable `import { mark } from '../../base/common/performance.js'` line and adds IStatusbarService, ICommandService, CommandsRegistry, ISearchService, IViewsService, and Registry imports.\n\nThis eliminates the AMD require() resolution at runtime which could fail in the WKWebView context, ensuring `__CEL_SERVICES__` is populated synchronously before the microtask queue drains. Also adds the `cel:services-ready` DOM event dispatch and Mountain diagnostic logging on success/failure.\n\nThe transform now includes a guard check for the import marker to avoid matching unrelated files.",
			"SHA": "ed06cce024f3c78dbd8db6ce7d842748a5094fa7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T21:47:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				221,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Route VS Code binary IPC channels to Mountain instead of stubs\n\nAdd MapChannelMethodToTauri, MapChannelToMountainPrefix, CoerceTauriParameters, and InvokeMountainRaw to route the VS Code workbench's binary IPC protocol (ChannelClient) to real Mountain backend handlers. Previously, channels like `localFilesystem`, `storage`, and `configuration` returned synchronous stub responses - filesystem ops returned FileNotFound, storage returned empty arrays, and configuration returned empty objects.\n\nNow these channels invoke Mountain asynchronously via the MountainIPCInvoke Tauri command, and the PromiseSuccess/PromiseError responses are relayed back through the binary IPC protocol. This enables the file explorer, search, settings editor, and workspace storage to persist data to the real filesystem and backend instead of operating on in-memory stubs.\n\nThe routing map covers 25+ channels: file, storage, configuration, search, workspaces, terminal, textFile, output, notification, progress, quickInput, environment, decorations, workingCopy, label, model, extensions, extensionHostStarter, localPty, nativeHost, themes, keybinding, lifecycle, url, menubar, encryption, and git.",
			"SHA": "67176ce21428951e8f07ce8a45ce3252ef478961"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T20:51:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				221,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Suppress benign ENOENT errors in Tauri invoke logging\n\nExtensions probe for optional workspace files (`.vscode/settings.json`,\n`.vscode/tasks.json`, etc.) that don't exist on fresh installs. Each probe\nwas logging a `tauri-invoke-error` entry, flooding the dev log with expected\nENOENT failures. Add logic to detect benign ENOENT errors for the\n`file:stat` and `file:readFile` methods by checking the error message for\n\"No such file or directory\", \"os error 2\", or \"Resource not found\" patterns.\nOnly non-benign errors forward to the log; legitimate errors still surface\nwhile harmless file probes stay quiet.",
			"SHA": "358f7f7c1c2c6c46b8c24f22cc1baaab6a18ab9a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T20:37:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				221,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Expose IViewsService and TreeViewByViewId in workbench accessor\n\nExtend the ExposeWorkbenchAccessor ESBuild transform to expose IViewsService alongside the existing Statusbar, Commands, CommandRegistry, and Search services. Add a TreeViewByViewId function that resolves ITreeView instances from the ViewsRegistry by viewId, mirroring MainThreadTreeViews.getTreeView() in stock VS Code.\n\nAlso separate error logging in TauriMainProcessService by tagging failed invokes with \"tauri-invoke-error\" instead of \"tauri-invoke\", allowing success logs to be opt-in via LAND_DEV_LOG while errors always forward.",
			"SHA": "7b0b915803bc81fd576b9f5236ee75d13d0b1052"
		}
	],
